f a clinical event monitor to prevent and detect medication errors. Proc AMIA Symp. 2000;640&#x02013;4.</citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Murff</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Patel</surname><given-names>VL</given-names></name><name><surname>Hripcsak</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bates</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Detecting adverse events for patient safety research: a review of current methodologies</article-title><source>J Biomed Inform</source><year>2003</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>143</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jbi.2003.08.003</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Murff HJ, Patel VL, Hripcsak G, Bates DW. Detecting adverse events for patient safety research: a review of current methodologies. J Biomed Inform. 2003;36:131&#x02013;43. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14552854</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Murff</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Forster</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Peterson</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Fiskio</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Heiman</surname><given-names>HL</given-names></name><name><surname>Bates</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Electronically screening discharge summaries for adverse medical events</article-title><source>J Am Med Inform Assoc</source><year>2003</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>339</fpage><lpage>350</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1197/jamia.M1201</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Murff HJ, Forster AJ, Peterson JF, Fiskio JM, Heiman HL, Bates DW. E